Description: Provides tools for importing, processing, quantifying, and visualising digital pain drawings. Pain drawings are commonly used in clinical research to document the location and distribution of pain on a schematic representation of the human body. Digital pain drawings can capture individual pen strokes as x- and y-coordinates, allowing more detailed analyses than traditional region-based classifications. The package supports the reconstruction of individual drawings, quantification of marked areas, anatomical region-based analyses, and the generation of group-level pain heatmaps. It is designed to work with data collected using the 'paindraw' REDCap external module, but also supports data from other sources.
